:null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in : v4.4-dev7, v4.3-stable, v4.2.1-stable(old)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.3.stable - Windows 10.0.26100 - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2050 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-12500H (16 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using a velocity related computation in _physics_process(), if you modify velocity using _unhandled_key_input() and are using event.is_action_pressed(), the computation only repeats around 31 times if you hold the key for longer than 31 frames(it repeats more or less times sometimes)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a scene with the following hierarchy:\n ```\n┖╴Node2D\n    ┖╴CharacterBody2D\n       ┠╴Sprite2D\n       ┖╴CollisionShape2D\n```\n2. Attach a script to CharacterBody2D with the following code:\n```gdscript\nextends CharacterBody2D\n\nvar speed = 200\nvar i = 0\n\nfunc _physics_process(_delta: float) -> void:\n\tif velocity.x != 0: #it works without this, but this block tells how many times the input is processed\n\t\ti += 1\n\t\tprint(i)\n\tmove_and_slide()\n\nfunc _unhandled_key_input(event: InputEvent) -> void:\n\tvelocity.x = 0\n\tif(event.is_action_pressed(\"ui_left\")):\n\t\tvelocity.x -= speed\n```\n\n3. Press the left arrow key for some time\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"RohitRao307","id":139103754,"node_id":"U_kgDOCEqOCg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139103754?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RohitRao307","html_url":"https://github.com/RohitRao307","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RohitRao307/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RohitRao307